# A step that writes a table and reads it back only to check it: the count decides whether `keep` throws and goes no
# further, so the table is where the route leaves its notes, in the codomain (mathematics.md, "A route's domain and
# codomain"; rule 4 of "The closed picture is the pushforward of the fine one"). The route is the module the `bin` runs.
# The library's operations whose result the body names are steps: `const db = new Database(..)`, and
# `const stored = db.prepare(..).get()`, which `db` goes into through the call it runs on.

route ledger.cli
step cli.ts/Ledger()
step cli.ts/Ledger.keep
step cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database()
step cli.ts/Ledger.keep/get

line entry > cli.ts call
line cli.ts/Ledger() > Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger() value
line Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger() > cli.ts/Ledger.keep value   # keep changes it itself (`this.kept +=`), and `Database()` takes it too
line cli.ts/Ledger.keep > Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger.keep value       # keep changes the ledger it runs on (`this.kept +=`)
line cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() > _·db@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() value
line Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger() > cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() value
line _·db@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() > cli.ts/Ledger.keep/get value
line _·db@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() > cli.ts/Ledger.keep value   # keep uses it itself (`db.exec`, `db.close`)
line cli.ts/Ledger.keep/get > _·stored@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/get value
line _·stored@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/get > cli.ts/Ledger.keep value   # keep checks the count itself
line cli.ts/Ledger.keep > SQLite(notes) own

home Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger() cli.ts
home Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger.keep cli.ts
home _·db@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() cli.ts/Ledger.keep
home _·stored@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/get cli.ts/Ledger.keep

# An error is a value (#121, decision 4): `Error(..)` makes it in the arm that raises it, and each border it crosses
# uncaught hands it on, up to the route.
choice cli.ts/Ledger.keep/?1
step cli.ts/Ledger.keep/?1/Error()
line cli.ts/Ledger.keep/?1/Error() > Error@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/?1 value
line Error@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/?1 > cli.ts/Ledger.keep value
line cli.ts/Ledger.keep > Error@cli.ts/Ledger.keep value
line Error@cli.ts/Ledger.keep > cli.ts value
home Error@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/?1 cli.ts/Ledger.keep
home Error@cli.ts/Ledger.keep cli.ts
line cli.ts > Error@cli.ts value                              # and the route's border hands it on, as `main`'s does in Rust
home Error@cli.ts cli.ts

side entry left
side SQLite(notes) right
